[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6177827175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124472#issuecomment-6177827175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124472","id":6177827175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcDopZw","user":{"login":"TrueJole","id":121569485,"node_id":"U_kgDOBz8AzQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121569485?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole","html_url":"https://github.com/TrueJole","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T20:32:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T20:41:26Z","body":"Can confirm on master (v4.8.dev.custom_build [d824ca9fe]). This does not seem to be a regression however, as It already occurred in the ancient 4.3 stable.\n\nIf you make add the gradient texture in the editor and set it like that, it looks correct.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6177827175/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6178067854","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124472#issuecomment-6178067854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124472","id":6178067854,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcD3Vjg","user":{"login":"b-28282","id":94022796,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZqsjA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94022796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282","html_url":"https://github.com/b-28282","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b-28282/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T20:45:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T20:45:39Z","body":"I think this is because a new Gradient initializes with two existing colors and offsets, `(0, white), (1, black)`. You can see 'em when you create one in the editor instead. The [docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_gradient.html) show these initial values as well.  \n\nBecause of that, when you add the two points, the gradient ends up with these values:\n`(0, white), (1, black), (0, white), (1, black)`\nwhich causes the weird behavior.  \n  \nIn general, I think you should clear out clear out the starting colors and offsets before adding your own, like this:\n```gdscript\n\tgradient.colors = []\n\tgradient.offsets = []\n```\nIf you do this, your gradient works just fine!\n\n---\nI have to add, this feels kinda counterintuitive? It makes sense to initialize the Gradient with those two values in the editor, but when created via code I'd expect it to be empty. \nCould it be possible to initialize a Gradient with empty values in code and with the two colors in the editor? I'm not familiar with the code :<\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6178067854/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]